%N A037665 Base 9 digits are, in order, the first n terms of the periodic sequence with initial period 3,1,0.
%H A037665 <a href="/index/Rec#order_04">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (9,0,1,-9).
%F A037665 G.f.: x*(3+x) / ( (x-1)*(9*x-1)*(1+x+x^2) ). - _R. J. Mathar_, Apr 30 2015
%F A037665 From _Elmo R. Oliveira_, Sep 20 2026: (Start)
%F A037665 a(n) = floor(9^(n+1)/26).
%F A037665 a(n) = 9*a(n-1) + a(n-3) - 9*a(n-4). (End)
%t A037665 Table[FromDigits[PadRight[{},n,{3,1,0}],9],{n,30}] (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Apr 29 2018 *)
%o A037665 (PARI) a(n) = 9^(n+1) \ 26; \\ _Elmo R. Oliveira_, Sep 20 2026
